 "transcript": [
  "[action] (to the eldest son, the second son) Wang Lung looks at his sons and then at Pear Blossom.",
  "[action] (to the eldest son) The second son returns home.",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"Well, and what now?\"",
  "[silence] (to the eldest son) Wang Lung says nothing.",
  "the eldest son (to Wang Lung): \"We will sell out the east fields, father, and I will buy more land in the west fields where the land is better.\"",
  "[action] Wang Lung feels the weight of his age.",
  "the eldest son (to Wang Lung): \"Well, and it is a good time for selling, for the land is fertile and the people are rich.\"",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"Well, and what then?\"",
  "[action] The eldest son buys more land.",
  "the eldest son (to the eldest son, the second son): \"Well, and now let us go and see the woman who has been chosen for my brother.\"",
  "Wang Lung (to the second son): \"Go, then, and may you be blessed!\"",
  "[action] Wang Lung sits and watches his son's wife.",
  "[action] (to the eldest son) Wang Lung expresses satisfaction with his son's wife.",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"She is fair and she is well enough shaped.\"",
  "[says] The eldest son responds with gratitude.",
  "the eldest son (to Wang Lung): \"Well, and it is a good thing and a relief to all of us, for you have been a lonely man and it is a comfort to see you with a young wife.\"",
  "[says] Wang Lung responds to his son's comment about his loneliness.",
  "[action] The sons dismiss the women and talk with their father alone.",
  "[action] The sons invite a younger woman to live with their father.",
